// register model goes stale silently, and then the testbench and the Linux
// driver disagree about the device.
//
// THIS IS NOT A FLAT uvm_reg_block, and that is deliberate (§8.2).
// Corundum's map is a WALKED LINKED LIST: each block carries its type, its
// version and the offset of the next one, and where a block LANDS depends
// on how the DUT was parameterised. Baking one build's offsets into the
// model would make it wrong for every other build, and would hide the very
// bug - a block missing or at the wrong offset - that walking the list
// exists to find.
//
// What is fixed, and therefore generated here, is the offset of each
// register WITHIN its block, plus the type IDs. Base addresses come from
